WEBVTT

00:00:01.450 --> 00:00:05.756
Every pay period has one week that matters most: the week before payday.

00:00:05.756 --> 00:00:08.447
Here is what your team does, and what you do.

00:00:09.797 --> 00:00:15.320
On Thursday at 8:00 PM Pacific, Workday automatically submits employee timecards.

00:00:15.320 --> 00:00:20.571
Before then, employees enter their expected hours for Friday and the weekend.

00:00:21.921 --> 00:00:26.727
Employees should not submit manually between 8:00 and 9:00 PM Pacific.

00:00:26.727 --> 00:00:30.710
A manual submit in that window can cause system conflicts.

00:00:32.060 --> 00:00:37.387
At 9:00 PM Pacific, timecards with overtime or on-call open for your review.

00:00:37.387 --> 00:00:42.364
Workday and email notify you when a timecard is over the standard week.

00:00:43.714 --> 00:00:50.797
On Friday of that week, you receive a reminder to approve your team's timecards before automatic processing on Sunday.

00:00:52.147 --> 00:00:58.840
Sunday at 2:30 PM Pacific is the last moment employees can correct Friday or weekend hours.

00:00:58.840 --> 00:01:01.341
Workday re-submits at that moment.

00:01:02.691 --> 00:01:07.662
Sunday at 6:30 PM Pacific is your final deadline to review and approve.

00:01:07.662 --> 00:01:12.142
Anything still unapproved is processed for payment as it stands.
